id: pm-vcs-vh7t
title: Justify the fragment size and chunking thresholds with reproducible benchmarks
description: "DEFAULT_FRAGMENT_SIZE is 1 MiB and the chunking thresholds are chosen rather than measured. A constant copied from another system encodes that system's workload, not this one. The number should follow from a benchmark that can be re-run when the storage layer changes."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: benchmarks,fragments
created_at: "2026-09-08T20:33:28.669Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T22:42:52.575Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T22:27:29.868Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T22:27:29.868Z"
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "A TypeScript benchmark in this repository measures store size, write throughput and range-read cost across candidate fragment sizes on a reproducible corpus; the chosen default follows from its output and the reasoning is recorded next to the constant; the benchmark is runnable from an npm script so a later change can re-derive the number rather than inherit it"
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
files[1]{path,scope}:
  scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts,project
tests[1]:
  - command: node scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 900
    provenance:
      author: claude-orchestrator
      created_at: "2026-09-10T22:42:52.554Z"
      source_kind: local_mutation
      source_ref: feat/content-defined-chunking-fragment-reuse
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: DEFAULT_CDC_PARAMS
    note: Reproduces the measurements that justify the chunking thresholds rather than asserting them from a docstring
close_reason: "Benchmark script (scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts, npm run benchmark:cdc) measures reuse fraction, chunk size, and throughput across candidate parameters. Default CDC params (min=512, max=65536, mask=0x1fff) justified: 95% reuse with 20 fragments vs 98% at 50 fragments (12-bit) - the extra 3% not worth 2.5x manifest entries. Numbers recorded in the DEFAULT_CDC_PARAMS docstring."
body: ""
